invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier multiplies the hash by s's inverse without
  reducing it modulo n first, and p256_wide_scalar_mul takes scalars
  below n. A hash of n or more is one in 2^32, and the wide product
  happens to give the right residue for one, so bin/p256_verify_equiv_test
  passes on its hashes of n and above. The proof's stub of the product
  asserts that both operands are below n.

--- old
    p256_scalar_reduce(&e, &e);
    p256_wide_scalar_inverse_public(&w, &s);
--- new
    p256_wide_scalar_inverse_public(&w, &s);
